      "problem": "What is $\\dfrac {2x + 4} {2}$ reduced to lowest terms?",
      "worked_solution": "We factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any factors that they have in common.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+4}{2} & =\\frac{2(x+2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{2}(x+2)}{\\cancel{2}\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+2}{1} \\\\  & =x+2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
